    <body>
      <div type="detail">
        <p>The Commonwealth Franchise Act 1902 granted voting rights to most men and women over 21, excluding Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people. Compulsory enrolment was introduced in 1911. Electoral rolls are available from 1903. Victoria stopped maintaining a separate State electoral roll on 31 January 1924 (the year compulsory voting was introduced), after which a joint electoral roll arrangement was entered into with the Commonwealth. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people gained the right to vote in Commonwealth elections in 1962. Federal electoral rolls include the name and address of the voter, their occupation, gender, and a registration number. The original records are held by the Australian Election Commission.</p>
        <p>Voters were listed in electoral districts and subdistricts according to their address. These boundaries could change over time. Relevant subdivisions include:</p>
        <list rend="bulleted">
          <item>Subdivision of Cardigan, Division of Melbourne</item>
          <item>Subdivision of Carlton South, Division of Melbourne</item>
          <item>Subdivision of Carlton, Division of Batman</item>
        </list>
        <div>
          <head>Data so far included</head>
          <p>1905	Division of Melbourne, Cardigan Polling Place</p>
          <p>1905	Division of Northern Melbourne, Carlton South Polling Place</p>
          <p>1919	Division of Melbourne, Subdivision of Cardigan</p>
          <p>1919	Division of Melbourne, Subdivision of Carlton South</p>
        </div>
        <div>
